WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
Good morning Hank it's Tuesday. Hi

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.570
everyone else. I'm Rosie Anna. I'm John's

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.400
assistant. I'm also John and Hank's secret

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.500
london sister, as of way back when. So

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.880
Hank when people find out that I'm John's

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.530
assistant, especially because I live so

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.240
far away in London, the number one

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.190
question they ask is, "so what is it that

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.929
you do?" Today I'm going to endeavour to

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:17.850
answer this question, but first I want to

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.020
give a little bit of an office tour,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.310
because we've seen your office in

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.050
Missoula, Hank, we've also seen Johns

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.550
office in Indianapolis. That's a really

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.689
hard phrase to say. Office in

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:26.939
Indianapolis. So without further ado, this

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:30.660
is my office. This is my view. These are

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.309
the wild animals I can see from my

00:00:32.309 --> 00:00:35.790
office. This is the foliage I can see

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.989
from my office, and these are the trees.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.910
So for the job itself, a large part of my role is

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.800
scheduling, which is lucky, because i am

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.480
awesome at it, through the combined

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.820
wonder of: Craigslist, shared calendars on

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.129
gmail and skype credit, i'm able to

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:51.620
coordinate someone, to come in and

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.700
organise John's 'pizza John shirts' by

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.260
hues. Very important that they're in

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.539
rainbow order. "God I love rainbows." I also

00:00:57.539 --> 00:00:58.710
get someone to come in and sit in John's

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.719
car seat, to warm it up, um, for about 15

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:02.039
minutes every time before he wants to

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:03.359
take the car out. I would say I spend

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:04.799
about half my time here in the london

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:06.810
office, and I can meet about three days a

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.460
week to indianapolis. Hardest part about

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.869
this is, probably the, I don't know, say

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.369
eight hours, or so, that I'm over the

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:13.380
Atlantic ocean without any internet. This is

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.610
particularly difficult for doing my job,

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.290
especially because John often calls me

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.090
quite casually, throughout the day, to do

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.020
things like look up words in the

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.490
dictionary for him. Not necessarily for

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.720
his next book, just to complete the

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.490
crossword. He says it's not cheating if

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.590
he asks me. On the upside, my air miles

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.270
are awesome, and the crew at Virgin

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.619
Atlantic, really know how to make an

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:30.450
amazing gin and tonic. Another key part

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.310
of my role is security testing. I feel

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.450
like I'm kind of a pro at this, because

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.100
I've seen every episode of Homeland at

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.659
least six times. I also remember

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.500
everything that Nancy McNally - well that

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.380
just fell down - has ever said. Okay well

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.960
now that's - yeah well done Rosie Anna. So

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.700
just like the NSA, I do spend a lot of my

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.409
time hacking into John's personal

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.939
accounts online. Just to double check all

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:52.530
the security levels, and then I also

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:53.909
change all the passwords, every like,

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:56.250
three hours. When John takes us to DFTBA

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.960
con four, I changed that to change the

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.850
passwords to every 15 minutes, just to be

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.469
super safe. But otherwise my assistantship

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:03.000
is pretty normal. Standard stuff the role

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.100
like, washing and blow-drying John's used

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.990
tissues, um, so that he can reuse them in

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.910
the name of sustainability. And also

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.590
ghost writing fan mail from John, to

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.500
Steven Gerrard, and by fan mail, I mean

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.270
love letters. Out of all my roles. this is

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.220
the hardest for me, because I'm a die-hard

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.890
West Ham United fan. I have been known to

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.840
slip a few references to bubbles, into

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.250
these love letters. I will admit that

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.200
Stephen Gerrard is a very talented player,

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.910
for Liverpool Football Club, and even a

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.350
little bit handsome. But I do always

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.360
feel like I'm betraying my beloved irons.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.250
But I suppose they gave us Carol so

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.690
there you go. Some of the recent projects

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.340
I've undertaken in my spare time, include:

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.140
building up Henry and Alice's library for

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.240
the next 15 to 18 years. Taking them from

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.890
the Jolly Postman, right up to the

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.450
unbearable lightness of being. Another

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.680
thing I'm doing is overseeing the

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.600
construction of an exact replica of the

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.820
Globe Theatre, in John's back garden,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.590
mainly so his kids could see Shakespeare

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.850
as everyone was supposed to see

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.130
Shakespeare, standing up. Other priorities

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.840
include: building up John's Lauren Conrad

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.250
gift collection, with a smidge of

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.989
Benedict Cumberbatch and the adolescent

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:58.580
wolf program, just keep everyone happy.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.830
So okay jokes aside, it is honestly the best

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.030
job I've ever had. It's really cool

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.320
getting to work with you guys. It's

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.640
really been earnest, thinking and looking back

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.070
at me in 2006. I used to read John's blog,

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.100
his very static blog, and 2007 me who was

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.720
addicted to brotherhood 2.0. Because the

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.340
tools I use now, without even thinking

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.440
about it to do my job, just weren't

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.140
really possible then. Skype out and shared

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.330
calendars, on start emails, that tell me

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.920
that it's time for John to put more air

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.690
in his tires. Which he spells with an 'i'

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.640
which is weird. So basically what I'm

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.810
saying Hank, is that we're living in the

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.880
future, and I'm loving it. Thanks for

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.560
being awesome everyone, and Hank, I will

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.060
see you on Friday, bye.

